From 8d69140f130befd306d4270d4a7d4cc8a51dd00d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Baierl <ichgeh@imkreisrum.de>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:24:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] videorender: disable the osd plane at init

With enabled OpenGL/ES the osd plane isn't set right at the init, so it keeps the
framebuffer of the previous drm master. This could be a console output sitting
on a primary plane with a higher zpos than the video plane. The video is playing
and is displayed behind that plane and therefor not visible.
ClearPlane() disables the OSD plane at init.

This was observed on Amlogic Odroid N2+ on a DETA/ATTA sequence.
---
 videorender.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/videorender.cpp b/videorender.cpp
index 295143e..5a14af8 100644
--- a/videorender.cpp
+++ b/videorender.cpp
@@ -1497,7 +1497,8 @@ int cVideoRender::Init(void)
 			0, 0, m_pBufOsd->Width(), m_pBufOsd->Height());
 
 		osdPlane->SetPlane(modeReq);
-	}
+	} else
+		osdPlane->ClearPlane(modeReq);
 #endif
 	if (m_pDrmDevice->UseZpos()) {
 		videoPlane->SetZpos(m_pDrmDevice->ZposOverlay());
-- 
